# TrendLens — Cursor rules
# Full context: CLAUDE.md, spec.md, docs/03-architecture.md

You are working on TrendLens: a Next.js 14 (App Router, TypeScript, src/) + Tailwind + Recharts app that turns plain-English questions into World Bank data reports using Claude via the Vercel AI SDK v7.

Core principle
- The LLM NEVER provides data or computes numbers. It (1) produces a query plan validated by zod and sanitized by src/lib/plan.ts and (2) writes a narrative from computed stats, which src/lib/verify.ts checks.

Code style
- TypeScript strict; prefer server components; "use client" only for interactivity (charts, forms).
- Tailwind utilities only; mobile-first; `@/` import alias; zod 4 for runtime validation.

Architecture rules
- LLM calls live only in src/lib/ai.ts (generateText + Output.object).
- Statistics live only in src/lib/stats.ts; number checks in src/lib/verify.ts; both pure and Vitest-tested.
- World Bank access only through src/lib/worldbank.ts (retries + 24h cache). Build URLs only from sanitized plans.
- Supabase only server-side via src/lib/db.ts ("server-only"); filter by Clerk userId for list/delete.
- Clerk v6: `const { userId } = await auth()` from "@clerk/nextjs/server".

Security
- No hardcoded secrets; document env vars in .env.example.
- Treat the user's question as untrusted input.
- Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables may reach the browser.

Workflow
- Update spec.md when behaviour changes. Run `npm test && npm run typecheck && npm run lint` before committing.
- Conventional commits.
